            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did nippu mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: గేదె",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గేదె (gēde) — \"a buffalo\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గేదె (gēde) is the water buffalo — black, unhurried, and the animal most of the పాలు in a Telugu household actually come from. The cow gets the songs; the గేదె (gēde) fills the pot."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is inherited, and the animal is so ordinary that arriving at a village house often means being met by one before anybody comes out to say నమస్కారం."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A గేదె (gēde) standing in a చెరువు with only its nose above the water is the picture the word carries. That is where it spends the hottest part of the day."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first animal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "gēde",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *gēde*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "gēde, then pālu, and say which one gives the other",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *gēde*, then *pālu*, and say which one gives the other]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does గేదె (gēde) mean? (\"a buffalo\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
