        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: మేక",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మేక (mēka) — \"a goat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మేక (mēka) is the goat: small, loud, and kept by households that cannot keep a గేదె (gēde). Where the buffalo wants water and grazing, the మేక (mēka) wants almost nothing and will eat what is left."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is inherited and it is old. Its shape sits close to the Tamil and Kannada words for the same animal, which is what happens to the names of animals people have kept for a very long time."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A మేక (mēka) will strip a bush bare and move on, which is why a గ్రామం keeps them at its edge rather than in its lanes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: one for milk, one for anything."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
