        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: చీమ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చీమ (cīma) — \"an ant\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చీమ (cīma) is the ant. After a గేదె (gēde) and a కోడి (kōḍi) it is a jump in scale worth making, because the same plain word-making covers whatever lives in a house, however small it is."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is inherited. Telugu has a stock comparison about a చీమ (cīma) carrying many times its own weight, and it is the ordinary way to praise somebody small who works hard."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A line of చీమలు across a floor usually ends at a పండు somebody left out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four: the biggest and the smallest so far."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
